pg"}, {"text": "<span class = \"strong\">Peter</span>: I see.</br>\n<span class = \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'm going to call them in a couple days if I don't hear back.</br>\n<span class = \"strong\">Peter</span>: Good idea. You have nothing to lose.</br>\n<span class = \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: The job ad said it was a full-time position.  You know I can only work part-time. What do you think?", "id": 2, "time": "18000", "image": "engenn4le18ob04re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "</br>\n<span class = \"strong\">Peter</span>: If you are the best candidate for the job, they might hire you anyway.</br>\n<span class = \"strong\">Peter</span>: You're going to use all those skills you learned at cooking school.</br>\n<span class = \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: That's right, and I can add the job to my resume. Employers always want to see that you have experience.</br>\n<span class = \"strong\">Peter</span>: True. Nice work, Vanessa. You're are always thinking ahead.</br>\n<span class = \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'm not just a pretty face.", "id": 3, "time": "35000", "image": "engenn4le18ob04re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa's Part-Time Job"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Opening Doors"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use information about personal and professional plans for the future in social and work situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le18ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Silent E"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are 5 spelling rules for the silent e."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rules\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1.A final e makes the vowel say its name.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cut, cute\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2.English words don't end in v or u.  The e after v or u does not affect pronunciation.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have, blue\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3.Silent e after the letter c and g \u201csoften\u201d their sounds.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rage, cabbage, face, experience\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"4. Every syllable must have a vowel. The final syllable can be pronounced without a vowel but every syllable must have a vowel.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tackle, pickle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"5. Sometimes the silent final e has no purpose.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"are, were\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "regardless"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in spite of difficulty"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are they going to consider you for the job regardless?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use in a conversation about jobs."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "not just a pretty face"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be attractive and intelligent "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm not just a pretty face."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nothing to lose"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when you cannot make things worse"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am going to talk to my boss because I have nothing to lose."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to think ahead"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to consider or think about the future"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are always thinking ahead."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob04aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to affect"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to cause a change"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The restaurant owner said it wouldn't affect my application."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob04aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chances"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an opportunity to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What are the chances of me getting a job here?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "skills"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to do something that comes from training, experience, or practice"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What skills do you have?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hire"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give work or a job to a person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you have experience, they might hire you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob04aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "candidate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is applying for a job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There were many candidates for the position."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and research a job you would like."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of the skills and qualifications you need for the job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write three sentences that explain why you are the perfect candidate for the job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the sentences to a partner. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about jobs online."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a list of skills and qualifications."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write sentences using skills and qualifications."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the sentences to a partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}